yamlover/structured
description: The one ordered container - keyed entries, positions, and a self-value mix
- >
  yamlover has ONE ordered container - there is no separate list and dict. Keyed and positional
  entries MIX in one node, a position is an integer key authored BY ORDER, and a scalar
  self-value may ride among the entries - the unified node (omni) is the DEFAULT, no tag
  needed. The spellings are YAML's -
  [block](::language:concretes:04-yaml:01-yaml_code:00-yaml_structured:00-yaml_mapping:00-yaml_mapping_block)
  and
  [flow](::language:concretes:04-yaml:01-yaml_code:00-yaml_structured:00-yaml_mapping:01-yaml_mapping_flow)
  - and a multi-line K&R flow token is a concrete SWITCH to
  [json5p](::language:concretes:05-json5p) mid-document. Flow cannot hold everything: a
  container carrying a bookmark, a `!!<...>` tag, a leading comment, a multi-line scalar, or
  a keyed+keyless mixture falls back to block form - silently and losslessly:
- !!<format: text/x-yamlover> |
  - solid
  scale: 10
  - recommended
- >
  The pair is a construct of its own - see the subchapter below:
- *: 00-yamlover_key_value_pair
